WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.378 --> 00:00:02.450
- B!
- It's not my fault!

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.290
- Why do you keep ripping
off the poor guy's right arm?

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.350
We don't need it.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.722
You've seen me play
Surgeon Simulator 1 before.

00:00:08.722 --> 00:00:10.330
(Mike yells)
Now It's time for

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.060
the brand new one that just
came out, Surgeon Simulator 2.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.960
But I need my handy side-kick.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.310
Welcome Bianca Antisera to the channel,

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.929
the pro gamer, the real life nurse.

00:00:19.929 --> 00:00:20.797
- What's up? Thank you
so much for having me.

00:00:20.797 --> 00:00:23.620
I am so excited to play
Surgeon Simulator 2.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:24.670
This is going to be awesome.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.680
It has been a very long time
since I have been in the OR,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.090
but I know we're going to destroy it.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.774
We're going to be like the dream team.

00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:32.370
(Mike yells)
Are you ready to come on

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.850
to the terminal with me?
- Yes.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.450
I brought you a cake. There you go.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.394
- Come. Oh, thank you.
- Oh, okay.

00:00:38.394 --> 00:00:40.360
- (grunts) That's what
I think of that cake.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.357
We're in, we're in.
(playful music continues)

00:00:42.357 --> 00:00:44.845
Oh, the diagnostic thing says heart.

00:00:44.845 --> 00:00:45.810
Does that mean we have to get the heart?

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.760
- Yes.
- Okay. I'm going to slam him

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.570
with this fire extinguisher.
- Okay.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.750
- Can you get the ribs out
of the way that I break?

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.583
- Yes.
(bones cracking)

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:53.930
- Did I break any off?
- You did!

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.470
Oh, we got the arm. The arm is off.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.580
- Wait, why did you take the arm off?

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.660
It's just supposed to be his heart.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.140
How can I get the heart
without getting the lung?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.253
- You're a little-
(bone cracking)

00:01:01.253 --> 00:01:02.086
(Bianca laughs)
- Oh, I got the,

00:01:02.086 --> 00:01:05.140
oh no, I got, I took the
lung out. I got his heart.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.090
- Ooh, he's bleeding out.
- Where does it go?

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.770
- Oh god.
- Where does the heart go?

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:08.900
- We need a new heart.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.930
- I don't know where to put it.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.404
Level failed, the patient
lost too much blood.

00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:13.237
(Bianca snorts)
Ready?

00:01:13.237 --> 00:01:14.380
I'm going to start breaking his ribs.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.330
- Okay. Let's go.
- Three, two, one,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.663
breaking ribs.
(bones cracking)

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.230
- Okay. We got one. Okay.
Let's get the, get the heart!

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.210
Let's go.
(bones cracking)

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.730
- I got the heart.
(machine beeps)

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.760
We need blood or we need
the stop bleeding medicine.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.780
I'm giving him the stop
bleeding medicine first.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:37.720
- I got blood syringe.
(bone cracking)

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.570
- Oh no, I cut his arm off!
- Oh my God.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.150
He's losing blood fast.
I'm getting another vial.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.510
- No! Why is he losing...

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.380
Oh, I got to put the arm back on.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.010
Come on! Okay. I put his arm back on.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:49.543
Are you getting another blood syringe?

00:01:49.543 --> 00:01:50.470
- Yes.
- I'm giving him

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:55.123
the stop bleeding medicine.
(playful music continues)

00:01:56.002 --> 00:01:58.120
(sighs) We left a tool in there.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.610
Let me get the tool out of here.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.163
Okay.
- I'll get it.

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:02.000
- Did we find the new heart yet?

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.187
- Maybe it's-
- Oh, I cut his leg off?

00:02:04.187 --> 00:02:05.420
- (laughs) Where is the heart?
- I put it back on.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.300
I put it back on. Not to
worry, I put it back on.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.610
Okay, here we go. I have organs here.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:11.680
What organ do we need? Heart.
- Yes.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.510
- I see a lot of organs but no heart.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.890
- If I was a heart, where would I be?

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.560
- Oh, I think I found an organ.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.940
- Oh, I found the heart! There
we go. There's the heart.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.723
I got the heart. Okay, let's go.

00:02:21.723 --> 00:02:23.850
(playful music continues)

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.943
I missed the stairs.
- We've come so far.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.483
Drop it in there. Yay!
(game chimes)

00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:31.208
- We did it! (laughs)
- He still has all the...

00:02:31.208 --> 00:02:33.492
High five, high five, high five.

00:02:33.492 --> 00:02:34.360
(Bianca yelling)

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.085
- We healed.
- We got an A.

00:02:36.085 --> 00:02:38.950
- Not that much blood
loss. Only six minutes.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.080
Let's go round two. There is no I in team.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.690
Wait, did it start already?
Oh no, what did it say?

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.540
- He's got two sick arms.
- Okay.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.110
I'm pulling off the right arm.
You pull off the left arm.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.930
- Okay.
- I ripped off his arm.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.300
Where does it go? Where does it go?

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.720
Quick.
- Oh my god.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.430
- Oh, we have to do one arm at a time.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.021
I almost feel like we're not
medical professionals, Bianca.

00:02:58.021 --> 00:02:58.910
(Bianca laughs)
- Where's-

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.130
- Okay. Which arm are we doing first?

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.470
Let's do right arm because it's
further away from the heart.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.296
- Okay. You do that. I'm going to get,

00:03:04.296 --> 00:03:05.740
I'm going to get the
thing to stop the blood.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.710
- The arm, this is the left arm, right?

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.890
No, I have the right arm.
(playful music continues)

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.710
Oh, no, it dropped.
(sad music)

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.700
- Okay. I'll keep them
stabilized til you get back.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.700
- I don't understand. I have
to put this arm somewhere?

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.840
I don't even know where.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.980
Do you see a place
where I can put the arm?

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.250
- I see where it goes, but
we're locked out of it.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.600
- You do! Where?
- Yeah.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.660
If you come back into the suite.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.090
- Oh, I'm in the bathroom.
Okay. I'm in here.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.660
- It's back here.
- Maybe there's like

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.370
a way to break in there or something.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.150
Oh, wait, I see what we need to do.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.265
We need to throw something up there.

00:03:37.265 --> 00:03:38.800
(suspenseful music begins)
- What if you pushed this box

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.580
and then I'll jump on it?
- You can do it, oh!

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.444
Oh, you were so close.
(Mike sighs)

00:03:44.444 --> 00:03:45.964
(suspenseful music continues)
(Bianca gasps)

00:03:45.964 --> 00:03:47.289
- Oh, I did it!
(game chimes)

00:03:47.289 --> 00:03:48.980
- You did it!
- Yeah boy!

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:51.219
I got his arm.
- Okay.

00:03:51.219 --> 00:03:52.430
(machine chimes)
- Okay, I did it.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.840
Okay, I found a healthy right arm.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.140
I'm coming. I'm coming.
(arm pops)

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.005
Okay. Right arm is on.
Let's get the left arm.

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:02.090
(bones cracking)
All right, the arm is off.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.470
I'm delivering it.
- I'm stopping the bleeding.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.805
- Okay. I got the left arm. I'm
coming in with the left arm.

00:04:08.805 --> 00:04:11.690
(yelling)
No, come on! There you go.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:15.045
(both yelling)
(game chimes)

00:04:15.045 --> 00:04:17.498
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!
- That was...

00:04:17.498 --> 00:04:20.699
I did not expect, man!
We didn't even get an A.

00:04:20.699 --> 00:04:22.590
We just passed. There's
like a pass or fail.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.917
- I have to rip off an arm
in order to get in here.

00:04:24.917 --> 00:04:27.236
Can I borrow your arm?
- Take it.

00:04:27.236 --> 00:04:29.234
- I can't. I don't think
it's your arm that I need.

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:30.901
Okay. What arm do you need?

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:32.448
Do you need a right arm or left arm?

00:04:32.448 --> 00:04:33.530
- Yeah, it's a right arm.
- Okay.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:36.390
Okay. I'm bringing it.
(playful music continues)

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.090
- Oh, it worked! I look like a hot dog.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.530
- Ah ha, I'm in.
- Don't mind if I do.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.070
- All right, left arm, right leg.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.964
I'm starting off with the left arm.

00:04:44.964 --> 00:04:45.797
(bones cracking)
All right.

00:04:45.797 --> 00:04:47.140
The right arm is off.
- Okay.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.370
- We have a problem.
(record scratches)

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.220
Look where the arm is. I can't get it out.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.860
- Oh no, oh no!
- Wait, Bianca,

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.204
try and press this button
that I'm looking at!

00:04:55.204 --> 00:04:58.912
(Bianca grunts)
Thank you.

00:04:58.912 --> 00:04:59.930
(machine chimes)
Okay.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.610
I have a healthy left arm for you.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.340
Bringing it in now.
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.570
- I'm bringing it!
- He's losing blood so fast.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.890
- I have, no no no. I have
the arm, I have the arm!

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.720
I put the arm back on!
(Bianca laughs)

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:12.670
Okay, so when I pull the arm off,

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.770
you have to go right
away with the syringe.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.130
- I got you.
- There you go.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:19.170
Okay. I ripped off his arm.
Open the door for me. Quick!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.850
- Okay. There we go. I'm
stopping the bleeding.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:23.810
Okay. Bleeding has stopped.
- Okay.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.630
I'm bringing the left arm in.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.730
Why won't the arm reattach, B?

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:30.280
- I don't know!
- Oh, I got it on. Okay.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.033
Did you rip off the leg?
- No.

00:05:32.908 --> 00:05:35.845
- It's the wrong leg!
- You have the leg, not me!

00:05:35.845 --> 00:05:36.890
I've got the syringe!
- Okay.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.540
I'm going to get the other leg out.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.720
- Okay. I got the blood.
(breathes heavily)

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.540
Don't panic. Don't panic.
Stay calm, stay calm.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.180
- I hope this is not how
you run codes in the ER.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.660
(bones crack)
- Oh my God.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:50.650
His arm popped off.
- No! Put it back on, B.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.140
- Oh my God. We're going to fail.

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:55.590
- B, why did you! I put his leg back! B!

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.290
Okay, I got the arm.
- All right.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.630
- I'm running to you now.
(playful music)

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.350
- This is it. I got faith in this one.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.930
- I'm on the way back with the right leg.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.470
Wait, why is his right arm off?

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:06.750
- Oh my God.
- B, put-

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.000
- I got it, I got it.
- Put his right arm back on.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.380
B!
- It's not my fault!

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.190
- Why do you keep ripping
off the poor guy's right arm!

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.610
We don't need it!

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.490
Okay. I've transferred
the leg for a healthy leg.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.120
- I'm stopping bleeding very gently.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.590
We have no limbs at this moment.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.230
- No limbs? What do you
mean there's no limbs?

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.470
- I mean none are removed

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.890
other than the ones that are necessary.

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:29.400
- So I'm going to pop in
the right leg right now.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.520
Boom. We saved him.
- What else does he need?

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.460
- Why isn't it not completed? Healthy...

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:36.225
Oh, we need to take out his appendix.

00:06:36.225 --> 00:06:37.710
- What?
- Or whatever

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.220
that blue thing is in the middle,

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:41.700
his small intestine I guess. I'll do that.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.733
Just keep him alive. Just stabilize him.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.200
- You got this, you got it. Perfect.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.960
- Okay, I took it off.
Where do I go with it?

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.510
- I have no idea. I'm
stopping the bleeding.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.110
Best wishes on your journey!

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.910
- Oh, I found it. I'm
running back with intestine.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:58.323
- We're looking good.
- Oh no, it fell.

00:06:59.722 --> 00:07:01.742
(game chimes)
Oh, we did it!

00:07:01.742 --> 00:07:04.262
- What!
- Yeah, good job.

00:07:04.262 --> 00:07:07.060
(Bianca yells)
Woo. Look at that dance.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.930
All right, let's beat
this and call ourselves

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.640
surgical simulation champions.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.690
How do you feel about these
dance moves right now?

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:18.430
Oh, look what I found.
- Wow. Dancing pays off.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.296
- What do we have to do?
- There's this place with,

00:07:21.296 --> 00:07:23.910
it looks like intestines
just like hanging out there.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.370
- Where?
- Yeah, rib pieces back here

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.190
that we can't get into.
- Oh yeah.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:29.210
But what is this thingy here?
- Looks like we gotta put

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:31.728
some battery.
- Oh, I see a vent.

00:07:31.728 --> 00:07:35.030
(playful music continues)
(Bianca gasps)

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:36.343
I'm in, I'm in it.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.490
I got it. I got an electric thing.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:42.830
- We might need it later. Cool.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.730
- All right. Now we can
go into the organ room.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.680
Okay, good, now that we've set this up,

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:49.210
let's start our operation, you ready?

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:51.690
- Yes. You know what? I
don't see any syringes here.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.700
- Forget syringes. I don't
know what we're doing here.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:54.990
- Oh yeah, we don't even have a screen

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.280
to tell us what's sick!

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.450
Oh wait, there's another one here.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:00.298
Let's see. There's another
little vent we didn't move.

00:08:00.298 --> 00:08:03.030
(grunts) Oh, we need another battery

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:05.380
to open up this red thing here.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.140
I guess this is where we're
gonna need our syringes.

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:10.453
I need my syringes!
- Get them.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:13.470
- Oh, wow.
- But I don't know what,

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.980
what surgery we're doing on him?

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:16.870
- When in doubt, replace everything.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:19.040
- Okay. I'm going to start
replacing stuff. You ready?

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.710
- All right. Bring it on.
(playful music continues)

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:24.180
Commencing rib removal. (grunts)

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:27.160
- Okay. Ribs are removed.
Now we need to...

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.344
Wait. Why'd you rip his arm
off? Put his arm back on.

00:08:30.344 --> 00:08:33.963
(bones cracking)
I took out his lung. No!

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.120
- Do you really think that we
have to replace everything?

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.210
- I don't know.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.670
All right. We need to
do his heart, stomach,

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:44.930
and right leg.
- Okay.

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:47.650
- Let's do his right leg
first. Okay. Left leg's off.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.810
- Stopping the bleeding, gingerly.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:52.440
(leg pops)
- Okay. Leg is on.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.520
- Oh my gosh. The syringe is

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.540
not wanting to cooperate with me.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:56.790
Here we go. Much better.
- You got this.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:58.240
I have faith in you.
- Yeah!

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.800
- Now I'm going to get his heart.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:01.810
But in order to get his heart,

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.546
I'm going to have to
break his ribs. Ready?

00:09:03.546 --> 00:09:06.850
- Yeah. There we go.
(bones cracking)

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.340
Uh oh.
- I took his stomach.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.368
